  "lead": "Public elementary and secondary enrollment was <b>49,387,403</b> in the United States in Fall 2024 (SRC-607-02). Massachusetts enrolled <b>915,932</b>, rank 17 of 51 (derived, SRC-607-02). The public high school 4-year graduation rate was <b>86.6%</b> in 2021-22 (SRC-607-03). Massachusetts was <b>90.1%</b>, rank 5 of 48 (derived, SRC-607-03). Out-of-school suspensions reached <b>1.32%</b> of U.S. public-school students in 2020-21; Massachusetts was <b>0.59%</b> (SRC-607-04). On the 2024 NAEP, grade-4 reading averaged <b>214.3</b> in the national public sample; Massachusetts scored <b>224.8</b>, rank 1 of 51 (SRC-607-05). Grade-4 math was <b>237.3</b> nationally and <b>246.5</b> in Massachusetts (SRC-607-05). Grade-8 reading was <b>256.7</b> / <b>268.0</b>; grade-8 math was <b>272.2</b> / <b>283.5</b> (SRC-607-05). NCES NPEFS current expenditures per pupil were <b>$17,644</b> in the United States in FY 2024 (SRC-607-06). Massachusetts was <b>$27,008</b>, rank 5 of 51 (derived, SRC-607-06).",
